# Express Auth

Better Auth integration for Express 5. Reference: [Better Auth Express docs](https://better-auth.com/docs/integrations/express).

## Mount handler

```typescript
import { toNodeHandler } from 'better-auth/node';
import { auth } from '@/lib/auth';

// BEFORE express.json()
app.all('/api/auth/*splat', toNodeHandler(auth));
app.use(express.json({ limit: '1mb' }));
```

Express 5 requires `*splat` wildcard syntax for catch-all auth routes.

## Session access

```typescript
import { fromNodeHeaders } from 'better-auth/node';
import { auth } from '@/lib/auth';

export async function getSession(req: Request) {
  return auth.api.getSession({ headers: fromNodeHeaders(req.headers) });
}
```

## What NOT to use

- **No** `nextCookies()` plugin
- **No** Next.js `headers()` or `cookies()` APIs
- **No** duplicate auth routes — Better Auth owns `/api/auth/*`

## CORS & cookies

- `cors({ origin: env.CLIENT_URL, credentials: true })`
- `trustedOrigins: [env.BETTER_AUTH_URL, env.CLIENT_URL]` in `auth.ts`
- `useSecureCookies: env.NODE_ENV === 'production'`
- `app.set('trust proxy', 1)` when `TRUST_PROXY=true`

## Rate limiting

- Apply rate limiter only to `/api/auth/*` paths
- Port `rateLimitAuth` from `src/lib/rate-limit.ts`
- Return 429 with `Retry-After` header when blocked

## Health check

- `GET /api/auth/ok` — verify handler mounted correctly after bootstrap

## Testing

- Supertest with `request.agent(app)` to persist session cookies
- Sign up: `POST /api/auth/sign-up/email`
- Sign in: `POST /api/auth/sign-in/email`
- See `tests/helpers/auth.ts`

